---
/**
 * The hero animation, "the line". One current carries typed work from several AI agents into one
 * business: bookings, orders, quotes and messages arrive as typed chips, land as rows, and are
 * decided by the owner's own rules and the owner's own AI. Four of the five are answered; one — the
 * quote — stops with an amber dot because a person is needed, which is what the product actually
 * does. Confirmed work carries on to the point of sale, the shop and the calendar. Those three are
 * drawn as a live link, never as a shipped logo, because the connectors are still being built.
 *
 * The timings are deliberate; do not retune them by accident.
 *  - TRAVEL is unequal per agent (1.34 / 1.16 / 1.42 s) so two arrivals never land on the same
 *    frame and the loop never reads as a metronome.
 *  - LOOP is 12.9 s against five items spaced 0.60 s to 8.65 s: long enough that the repeat is not
 *    noticed beside a headline, short enough that a visitor sees all four beats.
 *  - The return arc is inked only while an answer is travelling it (sd-trail, step 4). An always-on
 *    return line would claim a channel that is not always open.
 *  - The rule phrase holds for 1 s and fades over 0.42 s, so it lives 1.42 s. Decisions fall at
 *    2.38 / 4.41 / 6.74 / 9.01 / 10.43 s — gaps of 2.03, 2.33, 2.27 and 1.42 s. Exactly one phrase
 *    is ever on screen, but the last pair has no margin at all: it holds only because the gate is
 *    "ph >= p2 + .10", which can fire late and never early, and because say() rewrites the whole
 *    class in one call so no frame shows new text in the old tint. Widening that gap means moving
 *    the fifth item and therefore LOOP, which is a timing change and Tiago's call.
 *
 * The moving scene is built in JavaScript inside one <figure>, which is why the styles below are
 * global: Astro rewrites scoped selectors at build time, so they would never reach an element the
 * script creates at run time. Nothing leaks, because every selector begins with .sdf and every
 * keyframe is named sdf-*; the sd- class names exist only inside .sdf.
 *
 * The figure is not empty before that script runs. It ships with the scene at rest — the lines, the
 * card, the rule strip, the agents, the systems — server-rendered as inline SVG and dropped by
 * mount() the moment the live scene is ready. With JavaScript off, or if mount() throws, that
 * picture is what a visitor keeps, so the page can never show a hole where the hero is. The figure
 * also carries aspect-ratio 520/390, so the box holds its height from first paint and nothing below
 * the hero jumps. The static markup is generated from the same numbers the script uses
 * (build/gen-seed.js in the prototype folder); regenerate it rather than hand-editing it.
 *
 * Colours come from the site's tokens where one exists — --ground, --ink, --ink-2, --ink-3,
 * --hairline, --glass-bg, --glass-border, --row-bg, --c-booking/-ink and the rest, --ease-out-soft,
 * --font-sans, --font-display. The literals are only the fallback for a host that has not declared
 * a role alias, and night redefines those fallbacks under both the prefers-color-scheme query and
 * the [data-theme="dark"] attribute, the way the rest of the site does.
 *
 * Two day inks are a step darker than the brand's own: --c-message-ink #0b6a75 and --c-order-ink
 * #9c4409. At the lighter values the chip labels measured 3.97:1 and 4.22:1 on the day ground,
 * under the 4.5:1 floor, on the four words that carry the whole point. Both stay on their brand
 * hue. A host that declares these tokens itself needs the same two values.
 *
 * The pills are measured at run time (fit(), below) rather than hard-coded, so "Calendar" and
 * "Booking" cannot push out of their pills when Manrope loads or a fallback font resolves wider.
 * The pads used are the drawn ones, so where the metrics match the design the floor binds and the
 * composition is exactly as approved.
 *
 * With reduced motion the same machine is stepped forward to a composed still frame rather than
 * replaced by a second drawing, and the preference is honoured if it is turned on later.
 *
 * No max-width of its own: the piece is whatever its container is, and Hero.astro's .art-box
 * already caps it. The viewBox is 4:3, so a 900-wide instance is 675 tall, not 640.
 */
---

<figure class="sdf" role="img" aria-label="Several AI agents send one business typed bookings, orders, quotes and messages; the business's own rules and AI answer most of them automatically, while its point of sale, online shop and calendar are kept in step as those connections come online.">
<svg class="sd-seed" viewBox="0 0 520 390" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
<defs>
<linearGradient id="sdseed-g" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
<stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--sd-tangerine)"/>
<stop offset="58%" stop-color="var(--sd-flamingo)"/>
<stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--sd-violet)"/>
</linearGradient>
<clipPath id="sdseed-c"><path d="M188,105 A11,11 0 0 1 210,105 Z"/></clipPath>
</defs>
<g>
<path d="M56,104 C104,104 118,196 176,196" class="sd-line"/>
<path d="M56,196 L176,196" class="sd-line"/>
<path d="M56,288 C104,288 118,196 176,196" class="sd-line"/>
<path d="M344,196 C380,196 388,104 420,104" class="sd-line"/>
<path d="M344,196 L420,196" class="sd-line"/>
<path d="M344,196 C380,196 388,288 420,288" class="sd-line"/>
</g>
<!-- The two captions hang off the two margins, not off their columns: AI AGENTS starts at the
     left margin (30) and YOUR SYSTEMS ends at the right one (504). Left-aligning the right
     caption to its pills reads as hanging, because the caption is narrower than a pill row. -->
<text x="30" y="60" font-size="8.2" class="sd-cap">AI AGENTS</text>
<text x="504" y="60" font-size="8.2" class="sd-cap" text-anchor="end">YOUR SYSTEMS</text>
<g>
<rect x="176" y="76" width="168" height="240" rx="14" class="sd-glass"/>
<path d="M188,105 A11,11 0 0 1 210,105 Z" fill="url(#sdseed-g)"/>
<g clip-path="url(#sdseed-c)">
<rect x="187" y="96.4" width="24" height=".9" fill="var(--sd-ground)"/>
<rect x="187" y="98.7" width="24" height=".9" fill="var(--sd-ground)"/>
<rect x="187" y="100.8" width="24" height=".9" fill="var(--sd-ground)"/>
</g>
<text x="218" y="105" font-size="12.5" class="sd-title">Your business</text>
<line x1="188" y1="118" x2="332" y2="118" class="sd-hair"/>
<circle cx="176" cy="196" r="2.6" class="sd-port"/>
<circle cx="344" cy="196" r="2.6" class="sd-port"/>
<g class="sd-rule">
<rect x="188" y="126" width="100" height="19" rx="9.5"/>
<text x="198" y="138.6" font-size="8.6">Rules + your AI</text>
<circle cx="316" cy="135.5" r="3.2" class="sd-beat"/>
</g>
</g>
<g class="sd-agent" style="--ag:var(--sd-violet)">
<rect x="30" y="92" width="24" height="24" rx="7" class="bodyfill"/>
<rect x="30" y="92" width="24" height="24" rx="7"/>
<circle cx="37.6" cy="103" r="1.7" class="eye"/>
<circle cx="46.4" cy="103" r="1.7" class="eye"/>
<line x1="42" y1="92" x2="42" y2="85"/>
<circle cx="42" cy="82.4" r="2.6" class="ant"/>
</g>
<g class="sd-agent" style="--ag:var(--sd-lagoon)">
<rect x="30" y="184" width="24" height="24" rx="7" class="bodyfill"/>
<rect x="30" y="184" width="24" height="24" rx="7"/>
<circle cx="37.6" cy="195" r="1.7" class="eye"/>
<circle cx="46.4" cy="195" r="1.7" class="eye"/>
<line x1="42" y1="184" x2="42" y2="177"/>
<circle cx="42" cy="174.4" r="2.6" class="ant"/>
</g>
<g class="sd-agent" style="--ag:var(--sd-flamingo)">
<rect x="30" y="276" width="24" height="24" rx="7" class="bodyfill"/>
<rect x="30" y="276" width="24" height="24" rx="7"/>
<circle cx="37.6" cy="287" r="1.7" class="eye"/>
<circle cx="46.4" cy="287" r="1.7" class="eye"/>
<line x1="42" y1="276" x2="42" y2="269"/>
<circle cx="42" cy="266.4" r="2.6" class="ant"/>
</g>
<g class="sd-node">
<rect x="420" y="88" width="84" height="32" rx="10" class="pill"/>
<text x="462" y="107.4" font-size="9.4" text-anchor="middle">POS</text>
</g>
<g class="sd-node">
<rect x="420" y="180" width="84" height="32" rx="10" class="pill"/>
<text x="462" y="199.4" font-size="9.4" text-anchor="middle">Shop</text>
</g>
<g class="sd-node">
<rect x="420" y="272" width="84" height="32" rx="10" class="pill"/>
<text x="462" y="291.4" font-size="9.4" text-anchor="middle">Calendar</text>
